1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:03,251
Ravi reads a management book every night.

2
00:00:03,551 --> 00:00:04,526
Asha laughs.

3
00:00:04,526 --> 00:00:06,696
Managing is a gift, she says.

4
00:00:06,696 --> 00:00:08,193
Books can't teach it.

5
00:00:08,693 --> 00:00:09,928
Kabir disagrees.

6
00:00:09,928 --> 00:00:12,787
Management has rules, just like science.

7
00:00:13,087 --> 00:00:17,287
And Meena asks, why don't managers
need a licence, like doctors?

8
00:00:17,887 --> 00:00:21,451
So, is management an art,
a science, or a profession?

9
00:00:21,451 --> 00:00:22,849
Let's test all three.

10
00:00:23,549 --> 00:00:24,599
First, art.

11
00:00:24,899 --> 00:00:28,651
Art means using your personal
skill to get the best result.

12
00:00:29,001 --> 00:00:32,221
On Asha's day off, Kabir
uses her exact recipe.

13
00:00:32,221 --> 00:00:34,291
Same tea, milk, and sugar.

14
00:00:34,641 --> 00:00:36,846
But the customers can
taste the difference.

15
00:00:37,196 --> 00:00:38,096
Why?

16
00:00:37,702 --> 00:00:40,612
Asha has years of practice, cup after cup.

17
00:00:40,962 --> 00:00:44,014
On rainy days, she adds ginger on her own.

18
00:00:44,014 --> 00:00:45,260
That's creativity.

19
00:00:45,610 --> 00:00:47,384
So management is an art.

20
00:00:47,384 --> 00:00:50,841
Personal skill, practice,
creativity, and results.

21
00:00:51,441 --> 00:00:52,573
Next, science.

22
00:00:52,873 --> 00:00:55,788
A science is a systematic
body of knowledge.

23
00:00:55,788 --> 00:00:57,927
Tested facts, sorted in order.

24
00:00:58,277 --> 00:01:00,210
It works on cause and effect.

25
00:01:00,210 --> 00:01:02,040
Do this, and that happens.

26
00:01:02,390 --> 00:01:03,760
Ravi learns a rule.

27
00:01:03,760 --> 00:01:07,433
Give each person one clear
job, and the work gets faster.

28
00:01:07,783 --> 00:01:10,239
In physics, heat ice and it melts.

29
00:01:10,239 --> 00:01:11,562
Every single time.

30
00:01:11,912 --> 00:01:13,456
But people are different.

31
00:01:13,456 --> 00:01:16,209
A rule can work on
Asha, and fail on Meena.

32
00:01:16,559 --> 00:01:19,799
So management is a science,
but an inexact one.

33
00:01:19,799 --> 00:01:21,079
A social science.

34
00:01:21,679 --> 00:01:23,003
Finally, profession.

35
00:01:23,303 --> 00:01:27,243
A profession, like a doctor's
or a lawyer's, shows five signs.

36
00:01:27,593 --> 00:01:29,128
Specialised knowledge.

37
00:01:29,128 --> 00:01:30,465
Managers have it.

38
00:01:30,765 --> 00:01:32,433
Formal education.

39
00:01:32,433 --> 00:01:35,030
Colleges teach BBA and MBA.

40
00:01:35,330 --> 00:01:36,789
A professional body.

41
00:01:36,789 --> 00:01:39,970
In India, the All India
Management Association.

42
00:01:40,270 --> 00:01:41,629
A code of conduct.

43
00:01:41,629 --> 00:01:43,984
It exists, but it isn't compulsory.

44
00:01:44,284 --> 00:01:47,098
And a service motive,
society before money.

45
00:01:47,098 --> 00:01:48,129
Still growing.

46
00:01:48,479 --> 00:01:49,687
Here's the catch.

47
00:01:49,687 --> 00:01:52,711
Doctors and lawyers need
a licence to practise.

48
00:01:53,061 --> 00:01:54,659
A manager needs none.

49
00:01:54,659 --> 00:01:57,812
Ravi never passed an
exam to run Chai Corner.

50
00:01:58,162 --> 00:02:02,217
So management is only partly a
profession, still growing into one.

51
00:02:02,817 --> 00:02:03,953
So, who was right?

52
00:02:04,253 --> 00:02:05,521
Asha was right.

53
00:02:05,521 --> 00:02:06,573
It's an art.

54
00:02:06,873 --> 00:02:08,383
Kabir was right too.

55
00:02:08,383 --> 00:02:09,528
It's a science.

56
00:02:09,828 --> 00:02:11,483
And Meena found the gap.

57
00:02:11,483 --> 00:02:13,128
Only partly a profession.

58
00:02:13,478 --> 00:02:15,395
Science gives Ravi the rules.

59
00:02:15,395 --> 00:02:17,320
Art helps him use them well.

60
00:02:17,920 --> 00:02:18,820
Quick check.

61
00:02:18,793 --> 00:02:21,571
What does a doctor need
that a manager doesn't?

62
00:02:23,471 --> 00:02:24,391
A licence!

63
00:02:24,391 --> 00:02:27,213
Anyone can become a manager without one.

64
00:02:27,813 --> 00:02:28,826
So, remember.

65
00:02:29,126 --> 00:02:32,831
Management is an art: skill,
practice, and creativity.

66
00:02:33,181 --> 00:02:37,327
It's a science too, but an inexact
one, because it deals with people.

67
00:02:37,677 --> 00:02:39,565
And it's partly a profession.

68
00:02:39,565 --> 00:02:41,307
No licence is needed yet.

69
00:02:41,907 --> 00:02:45,861
Next time, we'll see if management
and administration are the same.
